<h3 class="qhw-cap" id="qnaphw-report-label">Report preview (anonymised; read-only)</h3>
<textarea id="qnaphw-report-text" aria-labelledby="qnaphw-report-label" class="qhw-report" readonly spellcheck="false" rows="22" placeholder="Click &quot;Collect report&quot;. It takes a few seconds; no drive is woken."></textarea>
<p class="qhw-p"><b>What is collected</b> (read-only, <code>scripts/qnaphw-report</code>): the Unraid and kernel versions, DMI names and BIOS version, CPU and memory size, <code>lspci -nn</code> and <code>lspci -tvnn</code>, the ids, subsystem, driver, links and PCIe error counters of every ASMedia, Marvell and QNAP device, the AHCI capabilities of each controller, the SATA ports with a link, each drive's model, firmware and path (no serial is read), <code>lsusb</code>, the hwmon sensor names, relevant <code>dmesg</code> lines and this plugin's view (units, bays, links, known issues). No drive is opened, so none can wake up.</p>
<p class="qhw-p"><b>Anonymiser</b> (<code>include/qnaphw-anon.php</code>): first the values this server knows are replaced (drive and USB serials, DMI serials and UUID, the hostname, users with uid 1000 and up, file system labels), then patterns catch the rest (MAC, WWN, UUID, LABEL= and UUID= values, IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, serial-number fields). The same value always gets the same placeholder. Read the preview before sending, and edit the downloaded file if you see anything you would rather not share.</p>
